==================================================================
DAY 32 - PART A: THEORY
Scheduling: nodeSelector, Affinity, Taints/Tolerations, DaemonSets
Time: 40-45 minutes
==================================================================

1. HOW THE SCHEDULER DECIDES
----------------------------
For each Pending pod:
  FILTER  remove nodes that can't run it (not enough requests,
          nodeSelector/affinity mismatch, taint not tolerated, port
          conflict, volume zone ...)
  SCORE   rank the rest (spread, least loaded, affinity preferences,
          image already present ...)
  BIND    write the best node into spec.nodeName


2. nodeSelector (simple)
------------------------
  k label node lab-worker disktype=ssd
  spec:
    nodeSelector:
      disktype: ssd
Pod only goes to nodes with ALL these labels.

Built-in node labels: kubernetes.io/hostname, kubernetes.io/os,
kubernetes.io/arch, topology.kubernetes.io/zone (cloud),
node.kubernetes.io/instance-type (cloud).


3. NODE AFFINITY (expressive)
-----------------------------
  affinity:
    nodeAffinity:
      requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:     # hard rule
        nodeSelectorTerms:
        - matchExpressions:
          - key: disktype
            operator: In           # In, NotIn, Exists, DoesNotExist, Gt, Lt
            values: [ssd, nvme]
      preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:    # soft, weighted
      - weight: 50
        preference:
          matchExpressions:
          - key: zone
            operator: In
            values: [a]

"IgnoredDuringExecution": if node labels change later, running pods
are not moved.


4. POD AFFINITY / ANTI-AFFINITY
-------------------------------
Place pods relative to OTHER PODS:
  podAffinity       "put me near pods with app=cache" (same node/zone)
  podAntiAffinity   "keep replicas of app=web apart" (HA!)
  topologyKey decides what "near" means:
    kubernetes.io/hostname         same node
    topology.kubernetes.io/zone    same zone

TopologySpreadConstraints is a newer, simpler way to spread evenly:
  topologySpreadConstraints:
  - maxSkew: 1
    topologyKey: kubernetes.io/hostname
    whenUnsatisfiable: DoNotSchedule    # or ScheduleAnyway
    labelSelector:
      matchLabels: {app: web}


5. TAINTS AND TOLERATIONS (node repels pods)
--------------------------------------------
Affinity ATTRACTS pods to nodes. Taints REPEL pods from nodes unless
the pod has a matching TOLERATION.

  k taint node lab-worker2 gpu=true:NoSchedule
  tolerations:
  - key: gpu
    operator: Equal
    value: "true"
    effect: NoSchedule

Effects:
  NoSchedule        new pods without toleration won't be scheduled
  PreferNoSchedule  try to avoid
  NoExecute         also EVICT running pods without toleration

A toleration ALLOWS, it doesn't ATTRACT. For dedicated nodes use taint
+ toleration + nodeAffinity together.

The control-plane node has taint node-role.kubernetes.io/control-plane
:NoSchedule; that's why your pods never land there. Nodes that fail
get node.kubernetes.io/not-ready:NoExecute; pods tolerate it for 300 s
by default, then get evicted and rescheduled.


6. DAEMONSETS
-------------
One pod on EVERY node (or every matching node). New node -> pod added
automatically. Used for node agents: kube-proxy, CNI, log shippers
(Fluent Bit), monitoring (node-exporter), security agents.
DaemonSets usually tolerate taints so they run everywhere.


7. MANUAL AND OTHER CONTROLS
----------------------------
  nodeName: lab-worker      bypasses the scheduler (debugging only)
  k cordon NODE             mark unschedulable
  k drain NODE              cordon + evict pods (maintenance)
  k uncordon NODE
  PriorityClass             important pods can preempt less important
  PodDisruptionBudget       limit voluntary evictions (drain) so N
                            replicas stay up


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Filter, score, bind.
- nodeSelector/affinity attract; taints repel; tolerations permit.
- Anti-affinity / topology spread = HA across nodes and zones.
- DaemonSet = one pod per node.
